"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="113" name="Google Shape;113;p16"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="304800" y="1524000"/><a:ext cx="8382000" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="Diagram illustrating the seven processes that affect the steady-state concentration of a protein. At the top of the diagram is a narrow, long rectangular line, labeled DNA and divided into three segments. From left to right, the first sixth of the line is shaded blue, followed by a black line that separates the blue from the next segment, which is tan-colored and labeled Gene (this makes up the majority of the line), followed by another black line that separates the Gene from the remainder of the line, which is shaded blue and similar to the length of the blue at the beginning. Below this line is an arrow pointing down. Next to it on the right is a white number 1 in a gray circle (all the numbers from henceforth have a similar structure), marked “Transcription initiation.” Below the arrow is a shorter version of the rectangular line previously described, but this time, the line is shaded green and yellow, and labeled Primary RNA transcript. The line is divided into 7 segments, each separated by a short black line the height of the rectangle. Starting from left is a short green segment, followed by a slightly longer yellow one, followed by a slightly longer green one, a shorter yellow one, a long green one, a slightly shorter yellow, and an extremely short green one. Below this an arrow pointing down, and to the right of it is the number 2 (similar to number 1 described previously), labeled, “Posttranscriptional processing.” Below the arrow is a rectangular line about half the length of the one described in step 2. The entire line is shaded green and labeled, “mRNA.” Next to it on the right is the number 3, which is labeled, “RNA stability.” Below that is an arrow pointing down and labeled 4 to its right; this represents “Translational regulation.” Another arrow to the right points away from “Amino acids” and curves inward to the arrow pointing down. These two arrow point to a purple and white globular mass, shaped like a thick backwards C; this is labeled “Protein.” Below the mass is an arrow pointing down and labeled 5, “Protein modification.” Below that is a structure similar to the protein described previously, but this time, there are red dots dispersed evenly throughout the structure; this is labeled, “Modified protein.” Below this structure is another arrow pointing down to 6, labeled, “Protein transport.” On the right of the modified protein, a line curves upward to the “Amino acids” text described at step 4; the curved line is labeled 7, “Protein degradation.”&#xA;" id="114" name="Google Shape;114;p16"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="5294325" y="1524000"/><a:ext cx="3849687" cy="5324474"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>